# SI reservation system

This project includes a Vercel-ready reservation flow and admin dashboard.

## Required environment variables

Set these in Vercel under Project > Settings > Environment Variables.

- SUPABASE_URL
- SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
- ADMIN_PASSWORD
- SESSION_SECRET
- ETH_RPC_URL
- BASE_RPC_URL
- ETH_TREASURY
- BASE_TREASURY
- REQUIRED_CONFIRMATIONS (set to 2)

Do not put secrets in the repo or in browser code.

## Supabase table

Create a table named `reservations` in Supabase:

```sql
create table public.reservations (
  id uuid primary key,
  created_at timestamptz default now(),
  updated_at timestamptz default now(),
  chain text not null,
  tier text not null,
  wallet_address text not null,
  treasury_address text not null,
  tx_hash text,
  amount_eth text not null,
  amount_wei text not null,
  status text not null default 'pending',
  status_message text,
  confirmations integer not null default 0
);

alter table public.reservations enable row level security;
```

Use a service-role key in the backend only. Keep the table access restricted to server-side usage.

## Vercel deployment

- Deploy the repo to Vercel as a Node project.
- Keep `index.html` public for the landing page.
- The admin dashboard is served from `/admin` and requires an authenticated session.
- Use environment variables in Vercel, not in GitHub.

## Notes

- The public reservation page and the admin dashboard are only as good as the configured RPC endpoints and wallet addresses.
- The server checks for exact native ETH transfers on Ethereum/Mainnet and Base.
- Treat the admin password and session secret as production secrets.
